<%# locals: (governance:, governance_pda:, config_governance:, table:, network:, readable:, known:) %>
<%#
  (2) THE PER-ACTION THRESHOLD TABLE — `GovernanceConfig`, seeds [b"governance"].

  THREE STATES, AND THEY MUST NOT RENDER ALIKE:
    * the PDA exists          -> these are the numbers the chain enforces
    * the PDA does not exist  -> the deployed program is pre-v0.26 and enforces
                                 a STRUCTURAL two through `validate_multisig`,
                                 which never reads a threshold at all. The table
                                 below is then what turf-vault `accepted` WOULD
                                 enforce, and is labelled as such.
    * the app's switch disagrees with the chain -> every transaction this boot
                                 builds is the wrong shape. Said loudly.
%>
<section class="card p-4 mb-6">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-1">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading">Signature thresholds, per action</h2>
    <span class="font-mono text-2xs text-muted break-all"><%= governance_pda %></span>
  </div>

  <% if governance.present? %>
    <p class="text-secondary text-sm mb-3">
      Read from the on-chain <code>GovernanceConfig</code>. These are the numbers
      turf-vault actually enforces.
    </p>
  <% elsif !readable %>
    <%# UNREAD IS NOT ABSENT. "The account does not exist, so the program is
        pre-v0.26" is a CLAIM, and under an unreachable RPC it is one this page
        cannot make. Saying it anyway would put a confident, unverified sentence
        about the program's version in front of an operator mid-incident — the
        exact species of claim this page was built to stop. %>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-warning/40 bg-warning/10 p-3 mb-3">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-warning-ink mb-1">
        The GovernanceConfig account could not be read on <%= network %>
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs text-secondary">
        So this page cannot say which program version is deployed — an unread
        account is not an absent one, and the difference decides which
        instruction shape a rotation must use. The table below is the SHIPPED
        DEFAULT table plus the program's floors; treat it as a reference, not as
        a reading of this cluster. The eviction console refuses to build while
        this is true.
      </p>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-warning/40 bg-warning/10 p-3 mb-3">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-warning-ink mb-1">
        No GovernanceConfig on <%= network %> — the deployed program is pre-v0.26
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs text-secondary">
        The account does not exist, so there is no per-action table on chain.
        What the deployed binary enforces instead is <strong>structurally two
        signatures</strong> for every governance action: <code>validate_multisig</code>
        takes exactly two distinct signers and never reads a threshold field.
        The table below is what turf-vault <code>accepted</code> would enforce
        once v0.26 is deployed <em>and</em> <code>init_governance</code> has run —
        it is a forecast, not a measurement.
      </p>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# ONLY WHEN THE CHAIN WAS ACTUALLY READ. With an unreadable RPC,
      `governance.present?` is false for a reason that has nothing to do with the
      switch, and this panel would accuse the operator's config of a mismatch
      that may not exist. %>
  <% if known && config_governance != governance.present? %>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-danger/40 bg-danger/10 p-3 mb-3">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-danger-ink mb-1">
        This app and the chain disagree about the program version
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs text-secondary">
        <% if config_governance %>
          <code><%= Solana::Config::GOVERNANCE_ENV_VAR %></code> is on, so every
          transaction this boot builds carries the v0.26 account list and a
          five-slot argument — but the chain has no <code>GovernanceConfig</code>.
          Run <code>init_governance</code> after the upgrade, or unset the switch.
        <% else %>
          The chain is running v0.26 but this app builds the v0.25 shape. Set
          <code><%= Solana::Config::GOVERNANCE_ENV_VAR %>=on</code> and restart.
          A three-slot argument cannot express the deployed signer set.
        <% end %>
        The eviction console refuses to build anything while this is true.
      </p>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-xs">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-subtle text-left">
          <th class="py-1 pr-2 font-bold text-muted">Action</th>
          <th class="py-1 pr-2 font-bold text-muted">Signatures</th>
          <th class="py-1 pr-2 font-bold text-muted">Floor</th>
          <th class="py-1 font-bold text-muted">Source</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% table.each do |row| %>
          <tr class="border-b border-subtle/50">
            <td class="py-1 pr-2 font-mono text-2xs text-heading"><%= row[:action] %></td>
            <td class="py-1 pr-2 font-bold text-heading tabular-nums"><%= row[:effective] %></td>
            <td class="py-1 pr-2 tabular-nums <%= row[:floor] > 1 ? "text-heading font-medium" : "text-muted" %>">
              <%= row[:floor] > 1 ? row[:floor] : "—" %>
            </td>
            <td class="py-1 text-muted"><%= row[:source] %></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-3 text-3xs text-muted">
    A <strong>floor</strong> is immovable: <code>set_action_threshold</code>
    refuses to store below it and <code>threshold_for</code> raises a stored
    value up to it on read. That is what stops three signatures lowering
    <code>update_signers</code> to two and handing the vault back to two
    agent-reachable keys the next day.
  </p>
</section>
